checks/sources.tsv:67:groove-meetings-2016	http://web.archive.org/web/20160305122806/https://www.groovehq.com/blog/how-to-optimize-remote-team-meetings	Alex Turnbull / Groove — "How We've Optimized Remote Team Meetings For Ultimate Efficiency", published 2016-02-18, archived 2016-03-05 (the capture closest to publication, chosen over a later 2018 capture because the later one silently redacted a named coach to "our coach" — the article text is otherwise identical), consulted 2026-08-06. Founder's own contemporaneous account of Groove's meeting rhythm: four earlier formats tried and abandoned or kept (no scheduled meetings, a weekly Monday call, an all-culture Friday call, an unstructured daily standup), the "9-person 45-minute" meetings that resulted, a video of 1-800-Got-Junk's own daily standup (nearly 20 people, under 7 minutes) that reset Turnbull's expectations, and the fixed, timeboxed, owned agenda structure adopted afterward. Founder's own account: weaker evidence class per §5, attributed as such in the prose. The 1-800-Got-Junk figures are Turnbull's secondhand relay of a video his business coach showed him, not sourced to 1-800-Got-Junk directly — flagged so the eventual draft attributes them two layers deep, not as this book's own verification of another company's meeting length.
