scripts/prompts/review-checklist.md:22:  block and a reading list (`CONTEXT.md §3`).
scripts/prompts/review-checklist.md:23:- **The counter-case is the book's honesty mechanism**, and it is a specific, narrow claim: the
scripts/prompts/review-checklist.md:24:  chapter's own advice, followed by capable people, failing. Not related-but-different, not "the
scripts/prompts/review-checklist.md:25:  idea aged badly," not "someone half-followed this and it worked out anyway."
scripts/prompts/review-checklist.md:29:  dated, sourced to an official body, and never derived from memory (`CONTEXT.md §5b`).
