  2516	**What the missing evidence would have to be.** A real, small, self-funded business — software or
  2517	otherwise, at the reader's scale — that can point to a specific dated agreement (a client contract,
  2518	a standard-terms document, an employment or contractor agreement, an insurance policy) and a specific
  2519	cost that followed from what that agreement did or did not say: a client withheld payment on a
  2520	liability clause, a contractor kept the IP because nothing was signed, an insurer denied a claim on a
  2521	technicality, or a standard-terms dispute was voided under art. 6:233/6:234 BW6 for lack of
  2522	terhandstelling. This is a narrower ask than most of this book's cases: it needs a **cost event**, not
  2523	just a company's existence, and small self-funded companies — true to the epic's own framing — do not
  2524	routinely publish that kind of story with figures attached. A next attempt should search specifically
  2525	for indie-hacker "here's what I got wrong in my contract" retrospectives and small-claims or
